{
  "id": "ep079",
  "duration": 52.684,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.953,
      "text": "One supergiant galaxy almost bridges the Milky Way and Andromeda.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.967,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.953,
      "end": 13.373,
      "text": "On June 19, 1790, astronomer William Herschel discovered this faint celestial smudge in the constellation Virgo.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "William Herschel01.jpg",
        "credit": "Lemuel Francis Abbott",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Herschel01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.967,
          "end": 8.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.467,
          "end": 13.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.373,
      "end": 21.518,
      "text": "Today, we know that smudge as IC 1101, anchored at the center of the Abell 2029 galaxy cluster.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Color cutout hst 06228 03 wfpc2 f702w f450w pc sci IC 1101.jpg",
        "credit": "Hubble Space Telescope - Hubble Legacy Archive",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Color_cutout_hst_06228_03_wfpc2_f702w_f450w_pc_sci_IC_1101.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.367,
          "end": 21.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.518,
      "end": 30.913,
      "text": "Recent ultra-deep observations using the Isaac Newton Telescope revealed its measured main body spans 1.7 million light-years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.533,
          "end": 30.9,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.913,
      "end": 39.058,
      "text": "Containing trillions of solar masses, this cosmic colossus grew into a monster by cannibalizing neighboring galaxies.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Interacting Galaxies Hubble.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, A. Evans (University of Virginia, Charlottesville/NRAO/Stony Brook University), and the Hubble Heritage Team (STScI/AURA)-ESA/Hubble Collaboration",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Interacting_Galaxies_Hubble.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 39.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 39.058,
      "end": 46.058,
      "text": "Faint plume-like outer remnants show that it is still actively devouring nearby galactic debris today.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Interacting Galaxies Hubble.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, A. Evans (University of Virginia, Charlottesville/NRAO/Stony Brook University), and the Hubble Heritage Team (STScI/AURA)-ESA/Hubble Collaboration",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Interacting_Galaxies_Hubble.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 39.067,
          "end": 46.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 46.058,
      "end": 52.334,
      "text": "That is why this supergiant galaxy is so massive it would almost bridge the Milky Way and Andromeda.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 46.067,
          "end": 52.7,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
